**Reasoning:**
- Previously only the single best greedy candidate was refined; a candidate that starts slightly worse can end better after hill-climbing. Refining all 6 candidates explores more of the search space at negligible cost (the runtime is ~1ms, so even a 10x increase is far below limits).
- Swap moves are essential when the worst GPU is memory-constrained: moving a model out may be impossible (no other GPU has room), but swapping a large model for a smaller one can still rebalance pressure. This directly targets the max-KVPR objective.
- The `if dst == src or improved: break` guard keeps the inner loop from continuing after an improvement is found, keeping the search fast.
